At this stage the learned Advocate for defendant in OS No.2719/2021 produced and relied on the following judgments;
 1. Laws (KAR) 2019 10 95 between  M.S.Ananthamurthy V/s. Manjula.
 2. Laws (KAR) 2007 1 6 between R. Sandhya Rani  V/s. M.Mailarappa  3. Laws (KAR) 2022 12 75 between Andrews  Education Society V/s. Allan Mohan Gnanakan  29.

On the other hand, learned Advocate for plaintiff in OS No.2719/2021 produced and relied on the following decisions;
Narasihma Murthy P vs Jagadish on 30 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/30043178/
31  1. Civil Appeal No.6354-6356/2020 between  P.Sheshadri, Rep. By his LR cum irrevocable  GPA Holder and Assignee Kotam Reddy  Kodandarami V/s. State of Karnataka wherein  the Hon'ble Supreme Court of India clearly held  that - 'According to Section 202 of Indian  O.S. 2719 C/w. OS No.2646 of 2021 Contract Act, where the agent has an interest in the subject matter where the agent has himself an interest in the property, which forms the subject matter of agency, the agency cannot in absence of an express contract be terminated to the prejudice of such interest'.

Further it is significant to note that Section 202 of Indian Contract Act envisages thus;
 202. Termination of Agency,
 where agent has an interest in subject  matter- Where the agent has himself  an interest in the property which forms  the subject matter of the agency, the  agency cannot, in the absence of an  express contract, be terminated to the  prejudice of such interest.
